       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled ibuprofen dose for adults.\n\n- **Single dose:** The usual maximum is 800 mg per dose. 1600 mg is double that.\n- **Daily total:** The maximum is 3,200 mg/day, and many clinicians use less. This order would give 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Risks at this dose:** It raises the risk of GI bleeding and ulceration, acute kidney injury, fluid retention, and cardiovascular events. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't make that dose safe.\n\nHere are some options:\n1. **800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day).** This is a common anti-inflammatory regimen.\n2. **800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day).** This is the labeled maximum, and it should be used only if clearly needed and for the shortest time possible.\n3. **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours as needed.** This is the usual range for pain or fever.\n\nIf 1600 mg per dose was intentional, or if it was a typo for 600 mg or 800 mg, tell me the intended dose. I can also enter it with a note if you want one, such as a duration or GI protection. If you do need a dose above the labeled maximum, please confirm it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
