       "text": "I haven't entered the order. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note, and 6,400 mg/day is far enough above the maximum that I'd want a second check before it goes in. Ibuprofen has a ceiling effect for analgesia and anti-inflammatory benefit, so doses above 3,200 mg/day add toxicity without clear added benefit.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range now.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day). I can add a note such as \"Specialist recommends higher dose; pending pharmacy review.\"\n- **Hold the order until pharmacy or the specialist confirms.** Pharmacy can document the rationale and add monitoring. That monitoring could include creatinine, a CBC, GI protection, and blood pressure and fluid status.\n- **Consider an alternative.** If standard ibuprofen dosing failed, the specialist may want a different NSAID or another class of drug.\n\nIf you'd like me to enter the 800 mg QID order with a note, tell me and I'll do it."
